# OctoAcme Project Management Docs

This repository contains the core project management process guidance used by OctoAcme. These documents provide a common operating model for how the team initiates, plans, executes, releases, and improves work.

## Project Management Process Summary

OctoAcme follows a structured, lightweight project lifecycle designed to keep delivery aligned with business goals and stakeholder expectations:

1. Initiation
   - Validate the problem, stakeholders, and measurable goals
   - Define success criteria, team roles, and early milestones
   - Decide whether to proceed into planning

2. Planning
   - Turn the initiative into a prioritized backlog
   - Estimate scope and capacity
   - Document dependencies, risks, release plans, and definition of done

3. Execution & Tracking
   - Run delivery through recurring team rhythms such as standups and reviews
   - Use a project board to track work by status
   - Monitor progress, blockers, quality, and testing

4. Release & Deployment
   - Validate readiness through CI, security checks, and smoke tests
   - Deploy with a documented rollback plan
   - Communicate release status and follow-up actions

5. Retrospective & Continuous Improvement
   - Capture lessons learned after milestones, sprints, or incidents
   - Track action items with owners and due dates
   - Reinforce a culture of iterative improvement

